  "security_implications": "data_in_prev_q holds AES intermediate values that are considered secret. The register is cleared on asynchronous reset, but once reset is deasserted and a value is loaded, it persists until overwritten or reset again. This could lead to leakage of sensitive material if the register is readable later (e.g., via debug or scan) without prior overwriting. The design relies entirely on external control to remove secrets.",
